# Frontend Rules

- Use functional React components and TypeScript.
- Keep page composition, feature logic, reusable UI, and API access separated.
- Organize code by feature: intake, dashboard, documents, review.
- Use React Hook Form with shared Zod schemas for forms.
- Use TanStack Query for server state; do not duplicate server state in local component state.
- Keep local state local; avoid introducing a global state library unless a real need is demonstrated.
- Never call OCR libraries or AI providers directly from the browser.
- Never put secrets in Vite environment variables. Anything exposed to the browser is public.
- Render OCR and LLM text as plain text; never inject it as HTML.
- Show loading, empty, success, validation, and error states.
- Make forms keyboard accessible with labels, useful errors, focus handling, and semantic HTML.
- Use responsive layouts and accessible color contrast.
- Do not display AI-generated content as verified clinical truth. Label it as AI-assisted and awaiting human review.
- Keep source references visible next to summarized facts.
